<article class="env-lemma" id="012J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/012J">Lemma <span data-tag="012J">12.23.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $(K, F, d)$ be a filtered differential object of $\mathcal{A}$. The associated spectral sequence </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
weakly converges to $H(K)$ if and only if for every $p \in \mathbf{Z}$ we have equality in equations (<a href="/tag/012H" data-tag="012H">12.23.5.2</a>) and (<a href="/tag/012G" data-tag="012G">12.23.5.1</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
abuts to $H(K)$ if and only if it weakly converges to $H(K)$ and $\bigcap _ p (\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d) \cap F^ pK + \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d)) = \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d)$ and $\bigcup _ p (\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d) \cap F^ pK + \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d)) = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
